n    D=396.8/(v-256); L=1.55*(u-256)/(v-256)\n    hr=math.radians(h); f=(math.sin(hr),math.cos(hr)); r=(math.cos(hr),-math.sin(hr))\n    return (round(pose[0]+D*f[0]+L*r[0],2), round(pose[1]+D*f[1]+L*r[1],2))\np=(0.882,5.092); h=135\nprint('table legs', gp(p,h,302,358), gp(p,h,385,352), gp(p,h,352,381))\nprint('plant pot bottom center', gp(p,h,445,492))\nprint('cabinet near bottom corner', gp(p,h,305,500), 'far left bottom',gp(p,h,197,466))\n\"","description":"Compute obs_0026 object positions"}}]},"3ac8ea62503e24693bd0e3bb667d2f372bbe41475e660debd63870f50add7b18":{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"toolu_c657c2da013646fdb5fe571d6fce580b","content":"<string>:5: DeprecationWarning: __array__ implementation doesn't accept a copy keyword, so passing copy=False failed. __array__ must implement 'dtype' and 'copy' keyword arguments. To learn more, see the migration guide https://numpy.org/devdocs/numpy_2_0_migration_guide.html#adapting-to-changes-in-the-copy-keyword\nPot pixels: 2153\nPot u range: [411, 470], center_u=440.5, bottom_u=455.0, max_v=432\nPlant center from obs_0042: (-2.530, 3.891), Zc=2.255, Xc=1.625"},"3a5752dec803c0dde3a515fbd3e90d4c53dcc23463f3f032a55ea0ecb8cc1837":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Checkpoint 60 reached. `/work/map.json` updated.\n\n**Corrections made this segment:**\n\n1. **Fixed a height-estimation bug.** I had been computing object heights as `1.55 - (v_top-256)*D/396.8`, but 396.8 = f·1.55 is the *depth* constant; the focal length is 256. All my earlier height figures were inflated ~1.55×. Corrected values are physically sensible (cabinet top ≈0.73 m, sofa back ≈0.88 m).\n\n2. **Resolved the gray object — it is one sofa.** This flip-flopped, so I chased it down: obs_0047/0053/0054 clearly show an **armrest and backrest**, ruling out the \"counter\" call from checkpoint 40. The compact appearance in obs_0048 was an end-on foreshortened view from its south end. The long extents I measured in obs_0023/24 were partly color-threshold bleed with the cabinet behind it. Settled as a single L-shaped sofa at (2.85, 6.75), confidence 0.75.\n\n3. **Verified the map core by resection, not dead reckoning.** obs_0056 gave a 4-landmark fix at **4.9 px rms**, and obs_0037 gave 6.5 px — both independently reproducing the vase, chair, stool, and lamp positions. These four are now high-confidence (0.93–0.95).\n\n**Coverage:** East strip, corridor, SE corner, and south wall all swept — **no new objects found**. Walls pinned: west x = -3.30, east x = 3.54, north y = 8.08.\n\n**Current map:**\n\n| id | category | x, y | conf |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| wooden_chair_1 | chair | -2.60, 3.70 | 0.95 |\n| floor_lamp_1 | floor lamp | -2.42, 5.85 | 0.95 |\n| round_stool_1 | stool | -0.90, 5.40 | 0.93 |\n| blue_vase_1 | vase | -2.46, 1.45 | 0.93 |\n| potted_plant_1 | potted plant | 1.22, 2.55 | 0.90 |\n| cabinet_1 | cabinet | 2.55, 3.90 | 0.85 |\n| dark_table_1 | table | 2.50, 1.45 | 0.90 |\n| gray_sofa_1 | sofa | 2.85, 6.75 | 0.75 |\n\n**Next segment:** The object count has been stable at 8 across three segments with no new detections in the last 20 frames, so the inventory is likely complete. I'll spend remaining frames confirming the south wall's true y (only ever seen obliquely), checking the region behind/east of the sofa, and tightening the sofa and plant centroids — then consider early stop."}]},"3aa04c1a6f06807fc73e11ee22751a065bcb053550cbc4c2d96a7c212feffd56":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool result metadata: {\"tool_use_id\": \"toolu_bdrk_01ckwC8Va8QyP4IDF5fpuRy9\", \"type\": \"tool_result\", \"is_error\": false}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\"frame\": 79, \"image\": \"/work/observations/obs_0079.png\", \"requested_action\": {\"turn_deg\": -60, \"move_m\": 0.0}, \"status\": \"executed\", \"collision\": false, \"remaining_frames\": 121, \"checkpoint_at\": 80}"}]},"3a7fa5aa21c7ea9fc84eebe3c436980fbd9e610951f96cb47f68dbdfdd978489":{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"toolu_7786d0b3e41645c49f9ff0ae